[{:db/id "q-22084/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "329c5b59-f1a8-5258-9cdc-ee0a08cb9158" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "86bb8250-5f0c-5be3-b3a3-84ddbdb998e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a7edc25f-0337-5652-99b8-0a7ce55deec0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "736be88a-d3d6-51bf-aa18-cbd21566dcdb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7c210bf4-a271-5a46-8887-cec1d9c180d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b5b007-851a-5efc-b630-78d7a6b2737d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22084/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-22084/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-22084/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22084/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-22084/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-22084/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22084" :question/id #uuid "648e472e-d530-5d5d-b8f5-fb9004bc624e" :question/math-academy-id "q-22084" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3}$ defined on $(0,\\infty ).$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}{x}^{-8/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-8/3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{-5/3}(4{x}^{2}-8x+4) & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{-5/3}{(x-1)}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point on $(0,\\infty )$ is $x=1.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=\\frac{1}{2},2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{{2}^{-5/3}})(\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{5/3}\\cdot {2}^{-2} \\\\  & ={2}^{5/3}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\cdot {2}^{-5/3}(2-1)^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2-5/3} \\\\  & ={2}^{1/3}>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=1$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-22084/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
